  "2026-10-20T20:09:42.472Z",codex-agent,"Fix and regression evidence pushed as bf7681eb4edd16cd61846a425e41b5583d21054a. After restoring the fixed function and rebuilding, the five new parser/integration cases pass 5/5 again with zero failures/cancellations/skips. Additional read-only native PostgreSQL acceptance passes SELECT 1 for all three actual Unix-socket forms with both source/built validators accepting them; the smoke fixture required explicit PGUSER and PGPORT defaults rather than the process defaults. Froze 436 tracked inputs outside pm records and generated changelog. Sequential full npm and Bun release validation uses fresh HOME and isolated Git identity; current CI run 39488719299 tests the same source head on Node 22 and 26. Local npm typechecks, lint, 0-percent duplication across 237 sources and 764 documented declarations pass; full suites remain in progress. PR body updated through the REST API after this gh installation refused its GraphQL Projects-classic lookup. No review-thread reply/resolution or new pm CLI/SDK defect."
  "2026-10-20T20:15:07.786Z",codex-agent,"Extended driver-conformance self-review found another concrete validator mismatch: repeated host query parameters use last-value precedence in pg-connection-string, but the preflight used the first value. Verified both false rejection (blank first host, valid final socket host) and false acceptance (valid first host, blank final host). Fixing shared host lookup with getAll(...).at(-1), adding two positive cases and the reverse-order invalid control, then renewing function-only reverts and full gates on the new head. The obsolete local npm run reproduced the existing 300-second built catalog timeout plus following source case failure and was stopped before changing source; those receipts belong to the earlier snapshot. No thresholds or deadlines changed."
  "2026-10-20T20:17:39.534Z",codex-agent,"Renewed FINAL-FUNCTION revert proofs retain all fixed tests and rebuild with npm run build:server. Restoring only databaseConfigIssues from incoming 14e869b makes node --test test/startup-socket-config.test.ts fail 0/6 and node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"credentialed empty-host\" test/startup-readiness.test.ts fail 0/1, each exit 1 on intended assertions. Independent self-review proof retains all socket support and restores only first-value host lookup: same socket command fails 3/6 (both repeated-host acceptance cases plus reversed-order invalid-host control), while original three socket cases pass. All proofs have zero timeouts, cancellations and skips. Fixed function restored and build regenerated; pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 passes 6/6, and the real-database integration selection passes 1/1 again. Will renew complete npm and Bun release checks in Node 22/26 CI on the new source head; no redundant local full run after the already reproduced shared-host catalog deadline. Runtime inputs will be re-frozen. Item remains in_progress and will be released after gate evidence."
  "2026-10-20T20:35:29.519Z",codex-agent,"Source head 4d7578b27b79ea73e0e92602506d0ba11a06e498 is pushed with repeated-host precedence fixed, and 436 tracked inputs outside pm records/generated changelog are frozen. Current CI run 39490885281: Node 26 complete job passes both npm run release:check and bun run release:check, each 715/715 tests, capacity 2/2, all 44 required sources, 92.62 statements/lines, 81.76 branches, 95.98 functions; unchanged thresholds. CodeQL passes on this head. Node 22 npm gate passes; its Bun gate remains in progress. Isolated native PostgreSQL stopped, no residual scratch server in this package worktree, and local scratch evidence retained. Local catalog timeout/source-case cascade remains separate from final-source CI acceptance. Full final receipts and claim release will follow."
  "2026-10-20T20:43:34.375Z",codex-agent,"FINAL review-round evidence: source 4d7578b27b79ea73e0e92602506d0ba11a06e498 passes CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/39490885281, complete npm run release:check AND bun run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26 with fresh HOME and isolated Git identity. All four gates: 715/715 tests; zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo; all 44 required sources; capacity 2/2; packed npm/native-Bun current/minimum consumers 4/4; zero production vulnerabilities; duplication 0 percent across 237 sources; 764 documented declarations; every remaining release check passed. Coverage statements/lines/branches/functions: Node22 npm and Bun each 92.62/92.62/81.76/95.12; Node26 npm and Bun each 92.62/92.62/81.76/95.98. CI strict tracker health, committed-dist freshness and CodeQL pass. Local earlier snapshot hit existing 300-second built catalog deadline and subsequent source-case failure; both exact cases pass in all four final-source CI gates, with no threshold/deadline changes. Final fixed linked socket tests pass 6/6 and real PostgreSQL credentialed-host integration 1/1; actual Unix-socket SELECT 1 smoke passes all three forms. Incoming-function revert fails 0/6 configuration tests and 0/1 integration; independent first-host-value revert fails 3/6 configuration tests while original three socket cases pass. Each proof rebuilds dist and fails intended assertions with zero timeout/cancellation/skip; fixed source/build restored. Final complete review refresh has one addressed-but-unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6ufsM1; latest CodeRabbit body PRR_kwDOSZgR5c8AAAABTTvM4w has no outside-diff section. Self-review additionally fixed repeated-host last-value precedence. No new findings. All 436 frozen tracked inputs outside pm records/generated changelog still match tested 4d7578b; remaining changes are append-only pm evidence and claim release. Native fixture stopped; no residual scratch server. Existing local managed-extension version skew, tracker advisories, disabled test-result recording and operator-managed raw-log retention remain separate; no new pm CLI/SDK defect found. Releasing claim; item remains in_progress and unclosed. No review-thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merge, release or hosted changes."
